  "id": "DrugBank_DB00563 - MONDO_5062",
  "verbalization": "Methotrexate is implicated in the pathogenesis of lymphoma through a series of interconnected pathways. The evidence suggests that Methotrexate is associated with B-cell neoplasms and non-Hodgkin lymphoma, which in turn are linked to Rituximab and ultimately to lymphoma. This indicates a potential role of Methotrexate in the development of lymphoma via its interaction with B-cell malignancies. The presence of a direct indication from Methotrexate to Lymphoma, through the intermediate of Rituximab, highlights a possible mechanism where Methotrexate may influence lymphoma development by targeting or modulating B-cell pathways. The integration of these pathways underscores the importance of Methotrexate in the context of lymphoma, particularly in cases where B-cell neoplasms are involved. The evidence supports a mechanism of action that involves the interaction of Methotrexate with B-cell malignancies, potentially leading to lymphoma formation.",
